# The committed OpenAPI document is compared BYTE FOR BYTE with a fresh build-time
# generation (tests/Contract). The generator always writes LF; with core.autocrlf=true a
# Windows checkout would rewrite this file as CRLF and the comparison would fail on a
# difference that is not in the document. eol=lf keeps the working copy what the generator
# writes. It does not hide a generator-emitted CRLF: that would still fail the byte compare.
src/Api/openapi/*.json text eol=lf
